 ## Repair a failed connection
 
+Use the named connection in user instructions; the assistant should resolve
+technical identifiers without requiring users to edit CLI configuration.
+
+| Observed state | Recovery |
+| --- | --- |
+| Confirmed not installed in the client | Recommend the existing app for this surface and connect it. |
+| Installed but disconnected | Enable/connect that existing app through its native sign-in action. |
+| Expired/rejected authentication | Reconnect the same connection. An old Auth0 grant may need renewed consent through Casdoor; test the actual grant before attributing cause. |
+| Tools unavailable, state unconfirmed | Check enablement, workspace/account, policy, app-detail fetch/network failures and fresh-chat tool exposure. Missing tools proves neither uninstall nor expiry. |
+
+Preserve connection identities, endpoints, callbacks and scopes. Do not request
+secrets in chat or switch credentials to bypass denial. Public OAuth discovery
+and cached tool definitions do not prove authenticated access. After reconnect,
+check protocol/capabilities and read the wiki through that exact connection. A
+token read does not establish app-backed OAuth readiness, and a native OAuth read does
+not establish app-backed readiness. Verify each client/surface separately.
+
